---
description: "Rules for LangChain and LangGraph agent development"
globs:
  - "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Package Manager
- Always use `uv` as the package manager (never pip or poetry)
- Initialize new projects with: `uv init`
- Install base dependencies with: `uv add langchain langchain-openai python-dotenv black isort`

## Project Structure
```
project/
├── .env                  # API keys and environment variables (never commit)
├── .gitignore
├── main.py               # Entry point
├── agent/                # Agent logic
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── agent.py
└── pyproject.toml        # Managed by uv
```

## Environment Variables
- Always load env vars using `python-dotenv`
- Never hardcode API keys in source code
- Always include a `.env.example` with placeholder values
```python
from dotenv import load_dotenv
load_dotenv()
```

## LangChain / LangGraph
- Always check https://docs.langchain.com/ for the latest API before coding
- Prefer LCEL (LangChain Expression Language) over legacy chains
- Use `langchain-openai` for OpenAI models (not the base `langchain` OpenAI integration)
- Prefer `ChatOpenAI` over `OpenAI` for chat-based models

## Code Style
- Formatter: `black`
- Import sorter: `isort`
- Always use type hints on function signatures
- Use descriptive variable names, avoid abbreviations
